answers.text:
I set up this value in mimoto-issuers-config:

mosip.certify.authn.allowed-audiences={ ‘<http://localhost:8091>’, ‘<http://keycloak.local:8080/realms/inji-poc-2/protocol/openid-connect/token>’, ‘account’ }

exactly matching the aud value that is present in the token. But I didn’t configure anything about the audience in Certify config files, Should I?

[@TomasOGTIC](/u/tomasogtic) `c_nonce` used in credential download is generated by auth server and returned in token response.  
As your auth server is `Ory`, can you please check that `c_nonce` is being added in token response?  
**For Inji Mobile,**  
To get it work with Inji, we need to add `c_nonce` inside access token. We are using this library to take care of authorization and get token response [GitHub - FormidableLabs/react-native-app-auth: React native bridge for AppAuth - an SDK for communicating with OAuth2 providers](https://github.com/FormidableLabs/react-native-app-auth)  
This library doesn’t give the c\_nonce available in parallel with access token. We have identified this recently and moved to custom logic to get token response. But to work with old code, we need to c\_nonce inside access token

**For Inji Web,**  
We can fix in mimoto and you can apply that patch locally.

Esignet reference for adding c\_nonce in access token as well as at root level

[github.com/mosip/esignet](https://github.com/mosip/esignet/blob/master/oidc-service-impl/src/main/java/io/mosip/esignet/services/OAuthServiceImpl.java#L239-L250)

#### [oidc-service-impl/src/main/java/io/mosip/esignet/services/OAuthServiceImpl.java](https://github.com/mosip/esignet/blob/master/oidc-service-impl/src/main/java/io/mosip/esignet/services/OAuthServiceImpl.java#L239-L250)

[`master`](https://github.com/mosip/esignet/blob/master/oidc-service-impl/src/main/java/io/mosip/esignet/services/OAuthServiceImpl.java#L239-L250)

```
239. tokenResponse.setAccess_token(tokenService.getAccessToken(transaction, cNonce));
240. tokenResponse.setExpires_in(accessTokenExpireSeconds);
241. tokenResponse.setToken_type(Constants.BEARER);
242. String accessTokenHash = IdentityProviderUtil.generateOIDCAtHash(tokenResponse.getAccess_token());
243. transaction.setAHash(accessTokenHash);
244. if(isTransactionVCScoped) {
